{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>You shall surely tithe.</b> This pericope is juxtaposed because it is forbidden to eat any unclean bird or unclean beast or carcass, and behold, in the case of meat and grain it is forbidden to eat consecrated food except in the chosen place." "<b>The yield of the field, year by year.</b> Rabbi Judah Halevi the Spaniard, of blessed memory, said that it is attached to 'your seed' [in the previous verse], and the meaning is: the seed that you brought out to the field. In my opinion it is according to its plain sense, and its meaning concerns the produce — that which the field yields. And if one were to argue that Scripture says היוצא [a participle that does not normally take a direct object with את], we have shown him [the example] 'העיר היוצאת אלף' (the city that goes out a thousand) and the witness 'תשאיר מאה' (you shall leave a hundred). And our Sages, of blessed memory, said that it is the second tithe. Know: if you begin from above, the one is head; and if from below, the tenth. And this is the sod of the firstborn and the tithe. Know that the one is not in the count, and likewise the tenth, for it is opposite the one — for it is head to the second grouping and end to the first grouping. And every root in calculation is adjacent to it, before it and behind it. And because the one and the ten are principals, and the middle ones are five and six — these are called circular — therefore the letters of the [divine] name are these four, and from them are the letters of the honored and awesome Name."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:29.828788230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}